---
title: Sweet & sour tofu
servings: 1
course: dinner
cuisine: Chinese
tags: dinner, supper
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/sweet-and-sour-tofu-51da0af.jpg?resize=440,400
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/sweet-sour-tofu
time: 25m
---

Heat half the @rapeseed oil{0.5%tbsp} in a #non-stick frying pan{} over a medium heat. Add the @extra-firm tofu{75%g} and fry for ~{5%minutes}, turning regularly, until golden brown on all sides. Remove to a plate with a slotted spoon and set aside.

Heat the remaining @&rapeseed oil{0.5%tbsp} in the #non-stick frying pan{} over a high heat. Fry the @onion{0.5} and @red pepper{0.5} and @garlic clove{1} for ~{5%minutes}, or until the veg begins to soften. Add the @pineapple{80%g}, @ketchup{1%tbsp}, @rice wine vinegar{1%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{0.5%tbsp} and @water{50%ml}, and simmer for ~{1%minute}, or until slightly reduced. Stir the tofu back into the pan.

Cook the @basmati rice{} following pack instructions. Serve the tofu in bowls with the rice and a sprinkling of @sesame seed{}.
